    "q-111250": {
      "dom_id": "step-q111250",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "The random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2},\\, & 0\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind $P(X>Y).$",
      "worked_solution": "If $f(x,y)$ is a joint probability density function for the random variables $X$ and $Y$ and $A⊂{R}^{2},$ then\n\n$$\nP((X,Y)\\in A)={∬}_{A}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nNotice that $f(x,y)$ is nonnegative in the region $D=[0,2]\\times [0,1],$ and the event $A=\\{X>Y\\}$ corresponds to a subset of $D,$ shown as the shaded region below:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14215348/assets/2db85950b4d45901d79c173f264173d0c38046b2f087d0a28c8d5c69f024e31f.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>Y) & ={∬}_{A}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={∬}_{A}\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\text{Area}(A) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-111250-a",
